In article <werner-060393171200@tol7mac15.soe.berkeley.edu>, werner@soe.berkeley.edu (John Werner) writes:

> When Asmodeus (or other named demons, or the Wizard, or the Quest bad guy)
> teleport away to heal, they (always?) teleport to the up staircase on the
> level.  So if you clear a path to the stairs, you can follow him when he
> teleports away.  He'll keep teleporting in and out as you make your way to
> the stairs, but once you get there, he won't be able to teleport away
> anymore.  He might still "escape upstairs" though, which means you'll have
> to repeat the whole thing again.

There's another trick here.  If the bad guy does escape upstairs, just
make your way to the up staircase, go up and wait on the staircase
until he comes to you.  You can then go back downstairs; he will
follow, and you will be standing on the up staircase blocking his
escape route.

